        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify blur event behavior when focused element is removed]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42864</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42864"/>
        <updated>2026-01-22T10:45:47.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178316747?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">###Description</p>
<p dir="auto">This change clarifies the blur event documentation to note that browser behavior differs when a focused element is removed from the document.</p>
<p dir="auto">Specifically, Chromium-based browsers fire a blur event in this case, while Firefox does not.</p>
<p dir="auto">###Motivation</p>
<p dir="auto">The page previously stated that blur is not fired when a focused element is removed from the document, which is only true for Firefox.<br>
This update prevents confusion by documenting the cross-browser difference reported in issue <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3823377990" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42801" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42801/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42801">#42801</a>.</p>
